  "context": {
    "product": {
      "id": 914549,
      "name": "Lemon Balm",
      "description": "<p dir=\"ltr\"><span style=\"white-space: pre-wrap;\">Lemon balm is used in many ways, including:&nbsp;</span></p><ul class=\"lexical-text-editor--list-ul\"><li value=\"1\"><b><strong class=\"lexical-text-editor--bold\" style=\"white-space: pre-wrap;\">Food</strong></b><span style=\"white-space: pre-wrap;\">:&nbsp;The leaves can be added to salads, soups, sauces, and vegetables, or used to flavor tea.&nbsp;The flowers can be candied or used as a garnish.&nbsp;Lemon balm oil and extract are used to flavor beverages, baked goods, and more.&nbsp;</span></li><li value=\"2\"><b><strong class=\"lexical-text-editor--bold\" style=\"white-space: pre-wrap;\">Medicine</strong></b><span style=\"white-space: pre-wrap;\">:&nbsp;Lemon balm has been used to treat a variety of conditions, including anxiety, stress, insomnia, and indigestion.&nbsp;However, there is little scientific evidence to support many of these uses.&nbsp;</span></li><li value=\"3\"><b><strong class=\"lexical-text-editor--bold\" style=\"white-space: pre-wrap;\">Insect repellent</strong></b><span style=\"white-space: pre-wrap;\">:&nbsp;Lemon balm has been used historically as an insect repellent.</span></li></ul>",
